cderun is a CLI wrapper tool that simplifies running commands
within a container. It separates its own flags from the flags
intended for the subcommand.

Usage:
  cderun [flags]

Flags:
      --add-host stringArray               Add a custom host-to-IP mapping (host:ip)
      --cap-add stringArray                Add Linux capabilities
      --cap-drop stringArray               Drop Linux capabilities
      --cderun-add-host stringArray        Override add-host setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-cap-add stringArray         Override cap-add setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-cap-drop stringArray        Override cap-drop setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-cgroupns string             Override cgroupns setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-config string               Override config setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-cpu-shares int              Override cpu-shares setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-cpus float                  Override cpus setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-cpuset-cpus string          Override cpuset-cpus setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-cpuset-mems string          Override cpuset-mems setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-device stringArray          Override device setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-diagnosis                   Override diagnosis setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-diagnosis-format string     Override diagnosis-format setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-dns stringArray             Override dns setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-dns-option stringArray      Override dns-option setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-dns-search stringArray      Override dns-search setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-dry-run                     Override dry-run setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-dry-run-format string       Override dry-run-format setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-engine string               Override engine setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-entrypoint stringArray      Override entrypoint setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-env stringArray             Override env setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-expose stringArray          Override expose setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-gpus string                 Override gpus setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-group-add stringArray       Override group-add setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-hang-timeout string         Override hang-timeout setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-hostname string             Override hostname setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-image string                Override image setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-init                        Override init setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-interactive                 Override interactive setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-ipc string                  Override ipc setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-log-format string           Override log-format setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-log-level string            Override log-level setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-log-timestamp               Override log-timestamp setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand) (default true)
      --cderun-memory string               Override memory setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-mount stringArray           Override mount setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-mount-all-tools             Override mount-all-tools setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-mount-cderun                Override mount-cderun setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-mount-cderun-path string    Override mount-cderun-path setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-mount-cderun-socket         Override mount-cderun-socket setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-mount-socket                Override mount-socket setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-mount-socket-path string    Override mount-socket-path setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-mount-tools string          Override mount-tools setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-network string              Override network setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-oci-runtime string          Override oci-runtime setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-pid string                  Override pid setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-pids-limit int              Override pids-limit setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-prefetch string             Override prefetch setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-prefetch-all                Override prefetch-all setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-privileged                  Override privileged setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-prune                       Override prune setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-publish stringArray         Override publish setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-publish-all                 Override publish-all setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-pull string                 Override pull setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-pull-backoff-base string    Override pull-backoff-base setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
      --cderun-pull-max-retries int        Override pull-max-retries setting (highest priority, can be used after subcommand)
